                                                           cs2013:hasMasteryLevel <http://purl.org/cs2013/MasteryLevel/Familiarity> ;
                                                           rdfs:label "Symmetric multiprocessing (SMP)" .


###  http://purl.org/cs2013/LO/The_core_tier2_hours_would_be_
<http://purl.org/cs2013/LO/The_core_tier2_hours_would_be_> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                    cs2013:LearningOutcome ;
                                                           cs2013:hasKnowledgeUnit <http://purl.org/cs2013/KU/Basic_Type_Systems> ;
                                                           cs2013:hasMasteryLevel <http://purl.org/cs2013/MasteryLevel/Familiarity> ;
                                                           rdfs:label "The core-tier2 hours would be profitably spent both on the core-tier2 topics and on a less shallow treatment of the core-tier1 topics and learning outcomes." .


###  http://purl.org/cs2013/LO/The_processing_topic_area_incl
<http://purl.org/cs2013/LO/The_processing_topic_area_incl> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                    cs2013:LearningOutcome ;
                                                           cs2013:hasKnowledgeUnit <http://purl.org/cs2013/KU/Processing> ;
                                                           cs2013:hasMasteryLevel <http://purl.org/cs2013/MasteryLevel/Assessment> ;
                                                           rdfs:label "The processing topic area includes numerous topics from other knowledge areas. Specifically, coverage of processing should include a discussion of hardware architectures, including parallel systems, memory hierarchies, and interconnections among processors. These are covered in AR/Interfacing and Communication, AR/Multiprocessing and Alternative Architectures, AR/Performance Enhancements." .


###  http://purl.org/cs2013/LO/The_purpose_of_requirements_en
<http://purl.org/cs2013/LO/The_purpose_of_requirements_en> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                    cs2013:LearningOutcome ;
                                                           cs2013:hasKnowledgeUnit <http://purl.org/cs2013/KU/Requirements_Engineering> ;
                                                           cs2013:hasMasteryLevel <http://purl.org/cs2013/MasteryLevel/Usage> ;
                                                           rdfs:label "The purpose of requirements engineering is to develop a common understanding of the needs, priorities, and constraints relevant ta software system. Many software failures arise from an incomplete understanding of requirements for the software to be developed or inadequate management of those requirements." .


###  http://purl.org/cs2013/LO/The_topics_listed_below_have_a
<http://purl.org/cs2013/LO/The_topics_listed_below_have_a> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                    cs2013:LearningOutcome ;
                                                           cs2013:hasKnowledgeUnit <http://purl.org/cs2013/KU/Formal_Methods> ;
                                                           cs2013:hasMasteryLevel <http://purl.org/cs2013/MasteryLevel/Usage> ;
                                                           rdfs:label "The topics listed below have a strong dependency on core material from the Discrete Structures (DS) Knowledge Area, particularly knowledge units DS/Functions Relations and Sets, DS/Basic Logic and DS/Proof Techniques." .


###  http://purl.org/cs2013/LO/The_topics_listed_here_are_rel
<http://purl.org/cs2013/LO/The_topics_listed_here_are_rel> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                    cs2013:LearningOutcome ;
                                                           cs2013:hasKnowledgeUnit <http://purl.org/cs2013/KU/Parallel_Architecture> ;
                                                           cs2013:hasMasteryLevel <http://purl.org/cs2013/MasteryLevel/Familiarity> ;
                                                           rdfs:label "The topics listed here are related to knowledge units in the Architecture and Organization (AR) knowledge area (AR/Assembly Level Machine Organization and AR/Multiprocessing and Alternative Architectures). Here, we focus on parallel architecture from the standpoint of applications, whereas the Architecture and Organization knowledge area presents the topic from the hardware perspective." .


###  http://purl.org/cs2013/LO/The_view_here_is_on_the_hardwa
<http://purl.org/cs2013/LO/The_view_here_is_on_the_hardwa> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                    cs2013:LearningOutcome ;
                                                           cs2013:hasKnowledgeUnit <http://purl.org/cs2013/KU/Multiprocessing_and_Alternative_Architectures> ;
                                                           cs2013:hasMasteryLevel <http://purl.org/cs2013/MasteryLevel/Assessment> ;
                                                           rdfs:label "The view here is on the hardware implementation of SIMD and MIMD architectures." .


###  http://purl.org/cs2013/LO/This_history_of_computing_is_t
<http://purl.org/cs2013/LO/This_history_of_computing_is_t> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                    cs2013:LearningOutcome ;
                                                           cs2013:hasKnowledgeUnit <http://purl.org/cs2013/KU/History> ;
                                                           cs2013:hasMasteryLevel <http://purl.org/cs2013/MasteryLevel/Assessment> ;
                                                           rdfs:label "This history of computing is taught to provide a sense of how the rapid change in computing impacts society on a global scale. It is often taught in context with foundational concepts, such as system fundamentals and software developmental fundamentals." .


###  http://purl.org/cs2013/LO/This_knowledge_unit_builds_dir
<http://purl.org/cs2013/LO/This_knowledge_unit_builds_dir> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
